  body: "# Forfeiture rule in the pensions guidance\n\n## Source-backed proposal\n\nThe captured guidance describes
    a common-law forfeiture rule applied to social security benefits where unlawful killing and an advantage arising
    from a spouse’s or civil partner’s death are in issue.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nNo allegation, guilt, unlawful
    killing or forfeiture is determined by this project. The source gives an own-rights pension example where no
    forfeiture question arises, and distinguishes murder, manslaughter and culpable homicide in Scotland. Current
    legislation and case law require specialist review.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 76001, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a81fada40f0b6230269a321/dmgch76.pdf#page=3).\n\
    - [DMG 76002, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a81fada40f0b6230269a321/dmgch76.pdf#page=3).\n\
    - [DMG 76003, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a81fada40f0b6230269a321/dmgch76.pdf#page=3).\n\
    - [DMG 76004, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a81fada40f0b6230269a321/dmgch76.pdf#page=3).\n\
    \n## Provenance and review\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of DWP guidance, not an official DWP document.
    All definitions and relationships are model-assisted and unreviewed. No individual eligibility, award, legal
    conclusion or executable rule is supplied.\n\nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, stated
    legal date and pension event date have separate meanings. PDF page numbers are one-based file positions; extraction
    may damage reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n-
    `dmg-vol12-ch76` — PDF SHA-256 `074f2d3f00d4886954d5cbd6ba2653ec407c1ff9f0160a0ca74d337227f9f542`; page-extraction
    SHA-256 `53eb7c5ec81ced813ac2faf2af9f772c5f3e9662112a7ef678dcb4daef0b73f8`.\n"
