  - target: term/pension-forfeiture-ut-determination
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source reserves determination of a forfeiture rule question to the Upper Tribunal, with
      historical limits on modification.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol12-ch76/0003
      quote: "76005   Forfeiture rule questions can be determined only by the UT1. Before 25.7.86, there\n     \
        \   could only be a decision whether or not the rule applied. If it did apply the claimant\n        was
        prevented from deriving benefit directly from the unlawful act. There was no\n        power to modify the
        effect of the rule2.\n                                                                  1 Forfeiture Act
        1982, s 4(1); TP (UT) Rules, Rule 26;\n                                                                \
        \                            2 R(G) 2/84(T); R(P) 1/84(T)"
      locator: DMG 76005
  - target: term/pension-forfeiture-benefit-scope
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The chapter identifies SP/RP and bereavement-related benefit contexts affected by a deceased
      person’s contributions.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol12-ch76/0004
      quote: "76008   The benefits most likely affected by the forfeiture rule are WB, BB, BSP, SP and RP\n    \
        \    based wholly or in part on a late husband's, wife's or civil partner’s contributions\n        (see
        DMG 76032 - 76033)."
      locator: DMG 76008
